# Architecture — {{.ProjectTitle}}

## Overview

**{{.ProjectTitle}}** is a **{{.Framework}}** project generated on {{.Date}}.

## Request Flow

```
Client
  ↓
HTTP Handler (internal/app/)
  ↓
Service (internal/service/)
  ↓
Repository (internal/repository/)
  ↓
Database (PostgreSQL via GORM)
```

## Layer Responsibilities

| Layer | Location | Responsibility |
|---|---|---|
| Handler | `internal/app/<domain>/handler.go` | HTTP binding, validation, response |
| Route | `internal/app/<domain>/route.go` | Endpoint registration |
| Service | `internal/service/<domain>/service.go` | Business logic |
| Repository | `internal/repository/<domain>/repository.go` | Data access |
| Model | `internal/model/` | Database entity |
| DTO | `internal/dto/<domain>/` | Request/response shapes |
| Factory | `internal/factory/factory.go` | Dependency composition |
| Config | `internal/config/` | Configuration loading |
| Middleware | `internal/middleware/` | Auth, logging, CORS |

## Directory Structure

```
.
├── main.go
├── internal/
│   ├── abstraction/   # Echo context, pagination
│   ├── app/           # HTTP handlers + routes per domain
│   ├── config/        # Viper config loading + typed structs
│   ├── delivery/      # HTTP orchestrator
│   ├── dto/           # Request/response DTOs
│   ├── factory/       # Dependency wiring
│   ├── middleware/    # Auth, CORS, rate-limit
│   ├── model/         # GORM models
│   ├── redis/         # Redis adapter
│   ├── repository/    # Data access layer
│   └── service/       # Business logic layer
└── pkg/
    ├── circuitbreaker/
    ├── database/
    ├── date/
    ├── pad/
    └── response/
```

## Key Design Principles

- Dependency flows inward: `handler → service → repository → database`.
- Dependencies are injected via `factory.Factory` — no global state.
- Secrets never appear in source; they come from environment variables or Vault.
- Config is initialized once via `sync.Once`.
- **Configuration Precedence**: `config.yml` (primary) → `.env` file in root project loaded via `loadDotEnv()` (fallback, format: `DB_HOST=localhost`) / OS environment variables → safe defaults in `internal/config/config.go`.
